==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈdɔlmɛt͡ʃɐ/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Dolmetscher.ogg|audio}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|tolmetsche|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|sla|de}} language; compare Proto-Slavic {{recons|tъlmačь||interpreter|lang=sla-pro}} (Russian {{term|sc=Cyrl|толмач|tr=tolmáč|lang=ru}}, Polish {{term|tłumacz|lang=pl}}), whence borrowed from a {{etyl|trk|de}} language; compare Proto-Turkic {{recons|tilmaç|lang=trk-pro}} (Turkish {{term|dil|lang=tr}}, Azeri {{term|til|lang=az}}).

===Noun===
'''Dolmetscher''' ''m'' (''pl'' Dolmetscher) '''Dolmetscherin''' ''f''

# [[interpreter]] (as opposed to [[Übersetzer]] ([[translator]]))

